														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4855269">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Containment Procedures, Description, Recovered Incident Reports, Email Transcript</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Dramatic, with some lighthearted moments between the dog and it’s handler</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Elevator&nbsp;Pitch</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Elevator&nbsp;Pitch</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This SCP is a former SAR (Search and Rescue) dog that is completely unaffected by fire and smoke. When irritated, the dog is also able to raise its internal body temperature to an unnaturally high level, allowing it to essentially burn those who come into contact with it and spit small sparks. Visually, the dog is a completely average looking dalmatian. Given that it was an SAR animal, the dog had a handler. However, the handler was entirely non-anomalous and ignorant of the animal's abilities. The dog and the handler were close with the local fire department and went on missions almost exclusively related to local fires and their aftermaths.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Central&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Central&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The central narrative of this SCP Article would be the history of the SCP’s life prior to containment. This would be told through the local fire department’s incident reports recovered by the Foundation, detailing calls the dog was used on and how the dog and it’s handler performed. The reports would be written by the dog’s handler and would detail their specific experiences working with the dog during the incident. The handler is entirely human and simply good at their job. The dog’s anomalous protection does not extend to them nor anything other than itself.</p>
<p>The dog is contained by the Foundation after it gives several children second and third degree burns. This happens because of an off-duty incident when the dog and it’s handler are approached by a mother and her three children while relaxing at a park. The handler is distracted talking with the mother, while the children entertain themselves with the dog. Eventually, the dog becomes irritated by the attention and attacks them, biting one child and barking at the rest. This would result in the bitten child having a severe third degree burn from the bite and the other two children having small second degree burns from the dog’s saliva, sprayed from its barking. This portion of the story would be told by a hospital’s incident report that is also recovered by the Foundation.</p>
<p>This incident is what alerts the Foundation to the dog’s existence. The dog is subsequently contained, with it’s handler and any witnesses to the incident are anesthetized.</p>
<p>The article would end several years after the dog is contained, with a researcher in charge of the animal noting its declining health and mental state. The researcher makes a request to their superiors to suggest the dog be used for SAR work once again, this time for the Foundation. This portion of the article is told through an email.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Hook/Attention-Grabber</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Hook/Attention-Grabber</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I want the reader to feel bad for this SCP. It’s just an animal born with powers it can’t quite control. The dog only wants to help people and be with its handler, but that can’t be because of the dangers present with its abilities.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;Notes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;Notes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My plan is to make this article fairly straightforward and short given that this is my first. I’m not expecting it to be greenlit quite yet, but I would appreciate any continued criticism or suggestion. In particular, whether the concept seems viable or whether I should rewrite the concept entirely.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

