<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> scpwiki.com is a website created by The Foundation where creative writers post articles and tales detailing a fictional universe populated by anomalous items, entities and groups of interest, with the SCP Foundation at the heart.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The Foundation created the website after online discussions of the SCP Foundation emerged, with the aim of protecting the masquerade by decieving people into believing it was fictional. However, a shift from SCP-507 reveals it to be anomalous, and responsible for creating events and anomalies in an alternate universe and its own SCP Foundation, leaving The Foundation to ponder if they are any different.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/ Attention-Grabber:</strong> I want to ask a question that (please correct me if I'm wrong!) I haven't yet seen on the site; what if the Foundation exists in our world, and the site is merely for readers to be decieved into believing it does not exist? It fundamentally links our world and the fictional world in a very literal way.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Again, I cannot say I am hugely well-read on the site, and so it is possible an article similar to this exists, for which I apologise- it is a coincidence. But I do believe that it has potential (and even considered storing it for when I had more experience writing and proposing it for 001, but I don't think it would stand its ground, and I'm impatient!).</p>

